WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:09.860
He was staring directly at me.

00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:14.540
I stole a glance while turning my head to see bloodshot eyes staring back at me.

00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:19.539
Hello and welcome to Al Dente Creepypasta.

00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:24.380
Horror stories cooked to perfection with a splash of red sauce.

00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:29.400
My name is CZ and I will be your server this
episode.

00:00:29.410 --> 00:00:33.370
I know it's been a while since the last one,
and I am going to try to put these out more

00:00:33.370 --> 00:00:37.030
often by doing some shorter episodes from
time to time.

00:00:37.030 --> 00:00:39.880
This is a story I wrote called Bus Creep.

00:00:39.880 --> 00:00:41.940
Let's dig right in.

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:51.640
I offered to help my friend move apartments
last night . She had rented a U-haul, so I

00:00:51.640 --> 00:00:55.280
decided to take the bus to her house so I
didn't have to worry about parking.

00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:58.210
That evening after work I went to the bus
stop near my apartment.

00:00:58.210 --> 00:01:02.039
The bus was mostly empty; there were about
8-10 passengers on board.

00:01:02.039 --> 00:01:04.500
I took one of the sideways seats near the
front.

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:08.300
Most of the passengers were near the front,
since there were plenty of open seats.

00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:12.090
There was one guy sitting in the dark at the
back of the bus who I noticed when I first

00:01:12.090 --> 00:01:13.190
sat down.

00:01:13.190 --> 00:01:16.870
I didn't think much of it, as you can pretty
much count on there being at least one junkie

00:01:16.870 --> 00:01:20.110
on every bus ride, I usually just try to ignore
it.

00:01:20.110 --> 00:01:24.390
Which I did, until I heard the guy get up
and walk to the front of the bus...

00:01:24.390 --> 00:01:25.390
Only...

00:01:25.390 --> 00:01:29.580
Instead of getting off, he stopped right in
front of me and sat down in the seat directly

00:01:29.580 --> 00:01:30.610
across.

00:01:30.610 --> 00:01:35.580
My first inclination is to not make eye contact,
but I didn't have to look him in the eye to

00:01:35.580 --> 00:01:36.580
realize...

00:01:36.580 --> 00:01:38.410
He was staring directly at me.

00:01:38.410 --> 00:01:42.690
I stole a glance while turning my head to
see bloodshot eyes staring back at me!

00:01:42.690 --> 00:01:46.881
He had on one of those long rim hats like
you'd see on a pilgrim at Thanksgiving, with

00:01:46.881 --> 00:01:50.070
two long black pony tails coming down over
both shoulders.

00:01:50.070 --> 00:01:53.200
He had a short black trench coat and black
pants.

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:57.650
But his skin was pale, and rough looking,
like white sandpaper.

00:01:57.650 --> 00:02:00.659
His messy facial hair almost constituted a
beard.

00:02:00.659 --> 00:02:04.060
But maybe what bothered me most was his clenched
teeth.

00:02:04.060 --> 00:02:08.280
I couldn't tell if he was really excited about
something or if the sight of my face made

00:02:08.280 --> 00:02:10.319
him furious without reason.

00:02:10.319 --> 00:02:12.560
I decided I wasn't going to wait to find out.

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:14.650
I got up and moved seats.

00:02:14.650 --> 00:02:18.530
He turned his head and continued to stare,
so I just got on my phone and tried to block

00:02:18.530 --> 00:02:19.640
him out.

00:02:19.640 --> 00:02:23.970
This worked for about 5 minutes until the
guy got up again and moved into the seat across

00:02:23.970 --> 00:02:25.310
the isle from me.

00:02:25.310 --> 00:02:28.250
Ok, now this was starting to make me nervous.

00:02:28.250 --> 00:02:31.510
My stop was coming soon and I was faced with
a predicament.

00:02:31.510 --> 00:02:34.260
Chances are he wasn't going to follow me off
the bus...

00:02:34.260 --> 00:02:36.140
But if he did, I'd be alone...

00:02:36.140 --> 00:02:37.920
And relatively defenseless.

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:42.640
But if I stayed on the bus, I felt like this
dude might be on the verge of snapping.

00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:46.779
After considering for another minute, I decided
I'd stand up unexpectedly and walk fast to

00:02:46.779 --> 00:02:47.969
get off the bus.

00:02:47.969 --> 00:02:52.230
Hopefully he'd be left behind if he even attempted
to follow.

00:02:52.230 --> 00:02:56.010
My heart rate increased as we got close to
my stop, but I tried to make it look like

00:02:56.010 --> 00:02:57.639
I'd be settled in for a while.

00:02:57.639 --> 00:03:00.079
When my stop was called I waited...

00:03:00.079 --> 00:03:04.090
One one-thousand, two one-thousand, three
one-thousand...

00:03:04.090 --> 00:03:06.670
Then I hopped up and exited the bus and fast-walked
away.

00:03:06.670 --> 00:03:09.469
I quickly heard the bus door close back behind
me.

00:03:09.469 --> 00:03:14.889
I looked back, thinking I'd be alone, but
what I saw was the creep, standing there as

00:03:14.889 --> 00:03:20.180
the bus pulled away, his yellowing teeth glowing
in the moonlight, that same maddening stare

00:03:20.180 --> 00:03:22.159
plastered upon his face.

00:03:22.159 --> 00:03:24.439
There was only one thing to do now.

00:03:24.439 --> 00:03:25.439
Speedwalk.

00:03:25.439 --> 00:03:28.359
I wasn't going to run unless he actually did
something threatening.

00:03:28.359 --> 00:03:30.939
I also gave my friend a call.

00:03:30.939 --> 00:03:32.529
*Phone ring.*

00:03:32.529 --> 00:03:34.919
"Hey, I'm here."

00:03:34.919 --> 00:03:35.919
I lied.

00:03:35.919 --> 00:03:37.549
"Can you meet me at the gate?"

00:03:37.549 --> 00:03:41.450
As I walked I made an effort not to make it
obvious that I was looking back.

00:03:41.450 --> 00:03:43.269
I kept up the fast pace.

00:03:43.269 --> 00:03:46.650
When I got to the first corner I snuck a look
back over my shoulder.

00:03:46.650 --> 00:03:48.719
The dude was right on me.

00:03:48.719 --> 00:03:52.019
If anything he was actually closer than he
was before.

00:03:52.019 --> 00:03:54.629
He was still walking, but breathing heavily
to keep up.

00:03:54.629 --> 00:03:56.200
I picked up my pace.

00:03:56.200 --> 00:04:00.290
I j-walked at the next intersection to prevent
him from getting any closer, and he followed,

00:04:00.290 --> 00:04:03.209
nearly getting hit by car to do so.

00:04:03.209 --> 00:04:04.769
Now I was getting scared.

00:04:04.769 --> 00:04:08.459
I moved into a jog, I was basically jogging
at this point anyway.

00:04:08.459 --> 00:04:12.709
I heard his keys jingle behind me, signaling
that he too had started running.

00:04:12.709 --> 00:04:14.779
I saw my friend waiting at the gate ahead
of me.

00:04:14.779 --> 00:04:16.530
I motioned to her to go inside.

00:04:16.530 --> 00:04:17.530
She got it.

00:04:17.530 --> 00:04:21.090
I ran through the gate and she swung it shut
behind me, just before that haunting face

00:04:21.090 --> 00:04:24.490
came up to the gate and stared through the
bars.

00:04:24.490 --> 00:04:28.820
Not knowing if he'd try to hop the fence,
I ushered her inside.

00:04:28.820 --> 00:04:31.980
After explaining that night's events to this
point, I was relieved to find out that the

00:04:31.980 --> 00:04:36.320
garage is connected to her building, and we
wouldn't have to go outside to load the van.

00:04:36.320 --> 00:04:40.600
There was one point where I thought I saw
the man's face again inside the building.

00:04:40.600 --> 00:04:44.560
The door between the hallway downstairs and
the garage is made of glass, and as someone

00:04:44.560 --> 00:04:49.040
swung it open ahead of us, I could have sworn
I'd seen the man from the bus in the reflection,

00:04:49.040 --> 00:04:51.730
causing me to freeze up in the middle of the
hall.

00:04:51.730 --> 00:04:55.920
However, when we actually looked in the parking
garage it was completely empty.

00:04:55.920 --> 00:05:00.320
At the time, it was easy to chalk this up
to my paranoia, me just jumping at shadows.

00:05:00.320 --> 00:05:05.280
But what happened later that night has sort
of thrown that into question.

00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:09.280
It took a couple hours to fill up the U-Haul,
and by the time we pulled out, it was getting

00:05:09.280 --> 00:05:10.280
pretty late.

00:05:10.280 --> 00:05:12.860
I sat in the front passenger's seat as she
drove.

00:05:12.860 --> 00:05:22.840
She used her clicker to open the sliding iron
gate.

00:05:22.840 --> 00:05:24.660
No sign of anyone on the street.

00:05:24.660 --> 00:05:27.510
As we pulled out, I looked left and right
down the sidewalk.

00:05:27.510 --> 00:05:31.700
Thankfully, the street seemed empty, perhaps
the guy had gone home.

00:05:31.700 --> 00:05:33.660
The rest of the night went pretty smoothly.

00:05:33.660 --> 00:05:37.980
We unloaded the boxes at her new place, celebrated
the completion of the move with a glass of

00:05:37.980 --> 00:05:40.410
wine, and I was on my way.

00:05:40.410 --> 00:05:42.280
My friend offered me a ride home.

00:05:42.280 --> 00:05:46.500
I wanted to take it, but knowing that they
charge by the mile for U-Hauls, and knowing

00:05:46.500 --> 00:05:50.400
that we were nowhere near where the incident
with the bus creep had taken place, I opted

00:05:50.400 --> 00:05:51.820
to take the bus again.

00:05:51.820 --> 00:05:55.220
We were actually closer to where I live now,
so I didn't mind.

00:05:55.220 --> 00:05:57.440
And so, I was on my way.

00:05:57.440 --> 00:06:01.500
I'll admit that the idea of that man's stare
hadn't left my mind as I walked alone to the

00:06:01.500 --> 00:06:06.240
bus stop, but logically I didn't expect to
see anything, and I didn't run into anyone

00:06:06.240 --> 00:06:07.770
on the way to the bus stop.

00:06:07.770 --> 00:06:11.160
When I boarded the bus, I made sure there
were no shady looking characters hiding in

00:06:11.160 --> 00:06:15.840
the back, and once again, took one of the
sideways facing seats near the front.

00:06:15.840 --> 00:06:21.060
That's when maybe the most haunting part of
any of this became a reality.

00:06:21.060 --> 00:06:25.760
Looking out the window, I saw the same man
from before, staring at me from beside the

00:06:25.760 --> 00:06:31.000
bus, standing right at the bus stop where
I'd been standing moments before.

00:06:31.000 --> 00:06:37.030
I have no idea how he could have tracked me
from her old apartment to her new apartment

00:06:37.030 --> 00:06:41.180
and now to the bus stop miles away from where
this all started.

00:06:41.180 --> 00:06:45.760
It seemed like slow motion while the bus driver
closed the doors, and the man made no attempt

00:06:45.760 --> 00:06:50.920
to board, his trenchcoat blowing in the wind
as he stared me all the way out of sight.

00:06:53.420 --> 00:06:55.970
That was the last I saw of the bus creep in
person.

00:06:55.970 --> 00:06:58.770
But since then, I've woken up three times
tonight.

00:06:58.770 --> 00:07:02.560
Each time, his face was piercing into my nightmares.

00:07:02.560 --> 00:07:06.980
I don't think I'll be taking the bus tomorrow.

00:07:09.680 --> 00:07:13.240
